{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794389808,"nonce":"+f71YNLHnGVdvdGbx7+Xst/38sA=","title":"An HDLL primitive taken as a value fails when called from a Thread.create thread in jit and hybrid modes","message":"Reported by the hxn session on Ash 0.1.17 (target/release/ash at 69f9d628). `--mode interp` and stock HashLink 1.15.0 run it correctly; `--mode jit` and the default hybrid mode raise, caught as a Haxe exception on the worker thread:\n\n    compiled worker reached unprepared JIT sentinel for findex 29\n\nRaised by `jit_stub_call_bridge` in crates/ash_interp/src/interpreter/mod.rs (the `fiber_is_worker_lane` branch, near line 3297).\n\nWhat the reporter established:\n- Calling the same primitive directly from the worker thread works in every mode.\n- Calling it through a Haxe lambda (`() -\u003e Native.live()`) made on the main thread works in every mode.\n- Only the primitive itself as a value (`var live:() -\u003e Int = Native.live;`) fails, whether or not the main thread called through that value first.\n- A pure-Haxe version with no HDLL (a stored closure, a Mutex, the same Thread.create + events.runPromised shape) works in every mode.\n\nReproduction (any HDLL with a no-argument primitive):\n\n    import sys.thread.Thread;\n\n    @:hlNative(\"counter\")\n    private class Native {\n        public static function live():Int\n            return 0;\n    }\n\n    class Repro5 {\n        static function main() {\n            var live:() -\u003e Int = Native.live;\n            var events = Thread.current().events;\n            events.promise();\n            Thread.create(() -\u003e {\n                var seen = -1;\n                var error:Null\u003chaxe.Exception\u003e = null;\n                try\n                    seen = live()\n                catch (e:haxe.Exception)\n                    error = e;\n                events.runPromised(() -\u003e {\n                    Sys.println(error == null ? 'worker thread: $seen' : 'worker thread failed: ${error.message}');\n                    Sys.exit(error == null ? 0 : 1);\n                });\n            });\n        }\n    }\n\nBuilt files on the reporter's machine: bytecode /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/hxn/target/counter-hl/repro5.hl, library counter.hdll beside it (primitive hlp_live, signature \"P_i\"). From that directory:\n\n    DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"$PWD:/Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/ash/target/release\" /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/ash/target/release/ash --mode jit repro5.hl\n\nExpected `worker thread: 0`; jit and hybrid print `worker thread failed: ...`.\n\nhxn is not blocked: its binding now calls the primitive through a lambda. Not investigated yet.","files":null}]}